    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "The two lever points in your legislation that create the biggest improvement, if you will, in Social Security's finances. is one, the increase in the taxable maximum, and the other was the increase in the retirement age. Together, they both generate about 50% each of the heavy lifting there. Is it your opinion that any reform plan going forward is going to have to have components of those two elements there, that it's just mathematically impossible to solve this problem without raising taxes and raising the retirement age?",
