    "turn_text": "was bipartisan. In fact, it was the first bipartisan legislation since 1983. I'm pretty proud of that. one of the democrats on the bills congress and jim cooper who's a blue dog democrat from national tennessee uh... he was it's a very courageous move for a democrat to say i'm willing to raise the age or change the cold and i was able to get him on because i adjusted the poverty level to a hundred twenty five percent so we were capturing a group of of people that he cared deeply about As far as back home, I did a series of town halls on this. And the town halls always started out kind of raucous where people were in opposition. But then as I walked through the plan and they began to see the numbers and I actually showed where our interest payments on the national debt would be. I undershot what the debt was going to be because I projected the debt being in 2027 somewhere around 28 trillion. But we're at 34 trillion. It's 2024. But I didn't know about COVID at the time. When I started to explain what was actually happening and that we've got a real problem here, all of a sudden grandparents and parents started shaking their head, yes. But what I had to do, Tori, and I'm sure you guys ran into this back in the 90s and 2000s, was dispel all the myths. So I would start my presentation by listing the myths. and then say, okay, I know you think this, but it's not true. And I would have to go through and dispel all those myths. And once I was able to dispel those, I could actually have a conversation with both Republicans and Democrats, older workers and younger workers and retired folks, and people began to say, finally, somebody's talking to us about this rather than talking at us.",
