    "turn_text": "You know, it's great that you mention that because we often visit the subject of immigration for reasons that you just mentioned on this program. And, you know, I get a form up at the UNH School of Law, Franklin Pierce School of Law, earlier this year on immigration reform. And people sometimes ask, well, why is the Concord Coalition getting involved in immigration or speaking out on the subject. And it's really because the demographics work against the budget and against the economy. And immigration is one way to address that for reasons that you mentioned. It doesn't mean you can't do border security at the same time. You have to do border security at the same time. But we need the workers and they want to come here.",
