    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Look at what Social Security was first started. There are around 50 workers, and here's another thing that people need to understand. When your payroll tax is withheld, it's not being withheld for you and your name. It is actually transferring from you to a current retiree. It's a true direct transfer payment. When it was first started, there were around 50 workers for each retiree. Today, there's just under three. So we've got a real demographics problem, which creates this arithmetic problem that I was facing back in 2016, which has now become almost catastrophic in its ability to fix this. And so it's going to take some real leadership out of the White House, and some members of Congress to actually care enough about not the generation that follows us, but two generations back. And we've got to think completely different about America today.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Social Security was originally established with approximately 50 workers per retiree.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The current ratio of workers to retirees is just under three.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Payroll taxes collected are directly transferred to current retirees.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a significant demographic shift affecting Social Security sustainability.",
        "confidence": 0.9
