  {
    "episode_id": 65119,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/6/5/65119.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "So Congress, when you started this conversation, you talked about how you opened every conversation with your constituents, but the list of social security myths. You felt like you needed to dispel the myths before you could go into the nuts and bolts of your proposal. We're heading, we're in an election year. We've got two people running for president. Voters are going to the booths. Voters are also asking questions of people that are running for president and running for senate and running for the house. So here's an opportunity to educate them. What are some of the, like, pick the top two myths about Social Security that you just want to get out there right now and say, these are false.",
