    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "I'm not sure there is a way around it because candidates are going to say whatever they want to say, and they're going to do whatever they want to do, but the power of incumbency is so strong. It's rare. It happens, but rare that someone loses in a primary, but it does happen. But I certainly wouldn't want to live my life based on a position of fear. I'm not going to do anything because I'm fearful. Who wants to live that way and who wants to work that way? And so part of this is you might be in the wrong job if you're that fearful of keeping it. And quite frankly, if you're that desperate to hold onto it, you're in the wrong job. I would say that as well. But it's only things like this where you get the parties to stand down are only going to happen. when you get all the players in a room together and say, for the good of the country, we have to do this. We don't any longer have an excuse, and we have to address it. And so we're going to be willing to lay down ours if you're laid down yours, and let's just figure out how we're going to move forward. But that takes real leadership, and it's going to take leadership from the White House. And on this topic, The White House is absolutely vacant on this as was President Trump.",
